---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { graph, person, breadcrumbs, ORG_ID, PERSON_ID } from '../lib/schema';
import { quotes } from '../lib/quotes';

const description = `About ${site.name} and founder ${site.founder.name}: Search Essence Optimization, lead generation and follow-up for high-value service businesses.`;
const schema = graph(
  { '@type': 'AboutPage', url: `${site.url}/about/`, name: `About ${site.name}`, about: { '@id': ORG_ID }, mainEntity: { '@id': PERSON_ID } },
  person(),
  breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]),
);
---
<Base title="About" description={description} schema={schema}>
  <div class="container narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
      <h1>Your clients aren't just searching to find you. They're searching to understand you.</h1>
    </header>
    <article class="prose" style="padding-bottom: 72px;">
      <p>
        {site.name} was founded in {site.founded} by {site.founder.name}. Since 2016 he has worked across
        nearly every part of growing a business online: paid media, SEO, web design, content, B2B and B2C sales,
        and ecommerce. The firm exists to put all of that to work for businesses where a single client is worth
        a great deal.
      </p>

      <h2>Search Essence Optimization</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        <p>“{quotes.lookWithin.text}”</p>
        <cite>{quotes.lookWithin.author}, {quotes.lookWithin.source}</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Owen describes SEO a little differently: Search Essence Optimization. Ranking still matters, but it is
        no longer the whole job. Prospects now ask Google and AI assistants detailed questions, and those systems
        try to understand who you are, what you stand for and who you serve before they recommend you.
      </p>
      <p>
        So the work starts by finding the essence of your brand: what you do best, who you do it for and why it
        matters to them. Then we express it clearly and consistently everywhere a prospect looks, so people and
        AI search reach the same understanding of you. Your future clients are already moving toward you with
        their questions. Our job is to meet them in the middle.
      </p>

      <h2>What we believe about winning clients</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Match the path to the intent.</strong> If someone asks for a guide, give them the guide right away on a simple page. Every extra step costs trust.</li>
        <li><strong>Respond fast, and stay human.</strong> Automation should make follow-up quicker and more consistent without making it feel automated.</li>
        <li><strong>Trust is decided before the first conversation.</strong> Your ads, website, emails and reviews should tell one consistent story.</li>
        <li><strong>Stories beat service lists.</strong> People remember how you helped someone like them far longer than a list of what you offer.</li>
        <li><strong>Fix the fundamentals first.</strong> Better follow-up and less friction usually do more than another campaign or another tool.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>
        Owen has run paid media and content for as many as 15 accounts at once, including B2B lead generation,
        and has built seminar and webinar campaigns that turn attendees into clients. He sets up the automation
        that keeps follow-up consistent, and he earlier helped ecommerce brands grow on Shopify and Amazon.
      </p>
      <p>
        He has been a featured guest on industry marketing podcasts, talking through website and SEO essentials,
        lead follow-up systems and the shifts reshaping how buyers find businesses. He also holds a full stack web
        development certificate, which is why this firm builds its own pages, workflows and tools instead of
        handing them off.
      </p>

      <h2>Why "Perseverant"</h2>
      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        <p>“{quotes.promontory.text}”</p>
        <cite>{quotes.promontory.author}, {quotes.promontory.source}</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Lead generation for high-value services compounds. Search pages gain trust over months, a campaign
        improves with every test, and a client relationship can pay off for years. The name is a reminder that
        results come from steady, intentional work rather than one big push.
      </p>
      <p>
        It draws on two writers who believed in quiet, steady work. Henry David Thoreau wrote that he had great
        faith in a seed and was prepared to expect wonders from one. Marcus Aurelius reminded himself each
        morning that he was rising to the work of a human being. Every client engagement starts as a seed, and
        we show up every day to tend it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we work with</h2>
      <p>
        We focus on <a href="/industries/">businesses where one client is worth a lot</a>: law firms, elective
        healthcare practices, home improvement companies, senior living providers, recruiting and staffing
        firms, and estate security firms. We are based in {site.location.city}, Ohio, and work with clients across the {site.areaServed}.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
